  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="f-12" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;12. &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;The following officers were appointed during the period: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:82.142%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.914%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:50.892%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:25.894%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Jayson Antolin &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Principal Financial Officer and Treasurer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;05/13/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:15pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The following officers resigned during the period:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:82.142%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.371%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:55.602%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:21.727%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Burton D. Cole &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Principal Financial Officer and Treasurer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;04/24/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Danika Yeager&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Vice-President&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;05/08/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Jayson Antolin &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Vice-President&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;05/13/2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:15pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="f-13" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;13.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-14" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Description of Business&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;ANR Pipeline Company (the Company) was incorporated in the state of Delaware on July 20, 1945. The Company is a wholly owned direct subsidiary of American Natural Resources Company (Parent) and an indirect subsidiary of TransCanada American Investments Ltd., TransCanada PipeLine USA Ltd. (TCPL USA), TransCanada PipeLines Limited, and TC Energy Corporation, collectively referred to as &#8220;TC Energy.&#8221; The Company&#8217;s 9,400&#8209;mile transmission system transports natural gas from producing fields located primarily in Texas and Oklahoma on its southwest leg and in the Gulf of Mexico and Louisiana on its southeast leg. The Company&#8217;s system extends to markets located mainly in Wisconsin, Michigan, Illinois, Ohio, and Indiana. The Company&#8217;s natural gas pipeline also connects with numerous other natural gas pipelines, providing customers &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;with access to diverse sources of North American supply, including Western Canada and the Rocky Mountain region, and to a variety of end&#8209;user markets in the midwestern and northeastern United States (U.S.). The Company also owns and operates regulated underground natural gas storage facilities in Michigan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In addition, the Company owns TransCanada USA Pipeline Services LLC (TransCanada USA), which is a wholly owned subsidiary of the Company that serves to allocate management, administrative, and other service costs to TC Energy&#8217;s U.S. pipelines (U.S. pipelines) and other businesses. All costs (including payroll, benefits, incentive compensation, employee expenses, office costs, lease expenses and other costs) charged to TransCanada USA are identified and charged to the operating entities (primarily the U.S. pipelines as well as relatively smaller amounts to other TC Energy companies) to which services are provided. No material residual costs remain on TransCanada USA.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company is regulated by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). The Company&#8217;s financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting regulations of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which are a comprehensive basis of accounting other than U.S. generally accepted accounting principles (U.S. GAAP). The most significant differences between U.S. GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) the classification of certain accounts on the Comparative Balance Sheet, Statement of Income, and Statement of Cash Flows and (2) all subsidiaries, including those that are 100% wholly owned subsidiaries, are reflected on the equity method of accounting whereas U.S. GAAP requires that all majority-owned subsidiaries be consolidated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;These unaudited financial statements have been prepared in accordance with interim period reporting requirements. Because this is an interim period presented using a condensed format, this report should be read along with the Company&#8217;s 2025 Annual FERC Form No. 2 audited financial statements which includes a summary of its significant accounting policies and other disclosures. The Company has made all adjustments that are of a normal recurring nature to fairly present its interim period results. Information for the interim periods may not be indicative of the Company&#8217;s results of operations for the entire year. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Contingencies &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company is subject to various legal proceedings in the ordinary course of business. The accounting for contingencies covers a variety of business activities, including contingencies for legal and environmental liabilities. The Company accrues for these contingencies when the assessments indicate that it is probable that a liability has been incurred or an asset will not be recovered and an amount can be reasonably estimated in accordance with ASC 450, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;. The Company bases these estimates on currently available facts and estimates of the ultimate outcomes or resolution. Actual results may vary from estimates resulting in an impact, positive or negative, on results of operations and cash flows. Other than those reflected in this section, the Company is not aware of any contingent liabilities that would have a material adverse effect on the Company&#8217;s financial condition, results of operations, or cash flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;b.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.13pt"&gt;Legal Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company is not aware of any material legal liabilities as of June 30, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;c.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Regulatory Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The FERC regulates the rates and charges for transportation of natural gas in interstate commerce. Natural gas companies may not charge rates that have been determined to be unjust and unreasonable by the FERC. Generally, rates for interstate pipelines are based on the cost of service, including recovery of and a return on the pipeline&#8217;s actual prudent historical cost investment. The rates and terms and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;conditions for service are found in each pipeline&#8217;s FERC-approved tariff. Under its tariff, an interstate pipeline is allowed to charge for its services on the basis of stated transportation rates. Transportation rates are established periodically in FERC proceedings known as rate cases. The tariff also allows the interstate pipeline to provide services under negotiated and discounted rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In April 2025, the Company filed a Section 4 Rate Case with FERC requesting an increase to its respective maximum transportation rates effective November 1, 2025, subject to refund. As of June 30, 2026, there was a refund provision of approximately $211.8 million, including interest of $6.3 million (December 31, 2025 - $0.3M) reflected in these financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company reached a settlement with its customers effective April 2026 and received FERC approval on July 27, 2026. As part of the settlement, there is a moratorium on any further rate changes until November 1, 2029, and the Company must file for new rates with an effective date no later than November 1, 2031. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Annual Redetermination of Transporter&#8217;s Use and EPC Charges, FERC Docket No. RP26-586 et al.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On February 27, 2026, as amended on March 2, 2026, the Company filed its annual Redetermination of Transporter's Use and EPC Charges to comply with the fuel and electric power cost determination provisions of Sections 6.1.87 and 6.34 of the Company's FERC Gas Tariff, Third Revised Volume No. 1. On March 25, 2026, FERC issued an Order which accepted the Company&#8217;s tariff records effective April 1, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Cashout Mechanism, FERC Docket No. RP26-807 et al.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On April 30, 2026, the Company made its annual filing to establish its Cashout Price Surcharge pursuant to the Cashout provisions of its FERC Gas Tariff. The Cashout Negative Price Surcharge was set at $0.0018 based upon the Net Negative Cashout Activity balance of $4,412,025. On May 25, 2026, FERC issued an Order which accepted the Company's Cashout Price Surcharge effective June 1, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;4. Long-Term Debt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's long-term debt outstanding consisted of the following:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:92.857%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:59.156%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:2.746%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:14.925%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:2.746%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:14.927%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;June 30,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;December 31,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="9" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;(In thousands)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4.14% debentures due June 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:6.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;position:relative;top:-3.5pt;vertical-align:baseline"&gt; (1)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#8212;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;240,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3.26% debentures due May 2029&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;100,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;100,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3.43% debentures due May 2032&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;300,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;300,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3.58% debentures due May 2034&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;200,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;200,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3.73% debentures due May 2037&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;200,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;200,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5.23% debentures due September 2031&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;250,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;250,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5.69% debentures due September 2035&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;350,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;350,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1,400,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1,640,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Less: Current maturities of long-term debt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#8212;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;240,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 7pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&#160;Total long-term debt, net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1,400,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1,400,000&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:45pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-9pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:45pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-13.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:6.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;position:relative;top:-3.5pt;vertical-align:baseline"&gt;(1) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On June 10, 2026, the Company repaid the $240 million 4.14% debentures, together with accrued interest of $5.0 million.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On July 3, 2025, the Company entered into a Note Purchase Agreement pursuant to which it issued $250 million of senior unsecured notes bearing interest at a fixed rate of 5.23% due September 2031 and $350 million of senior unsecured notes bearing interest at a fixed rate of 5.69% due September 2035. These senior unsecured notes were issued in September 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Certain of the Company&#8217;s debentures contain financial covenants that limit consolidated funded debt as a percentage of the Company&#8217;s total adjusted consolidated capitalization. All outstanding debentures contain covenants limiting consolidated funded debt to no greater than 70% of total adjusted consolidated capitalization. At June 30, 2026, the Company&#8217;s ratio of consolidated funded debt to total adjusted consolidated capitalization was 29.0%.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;As of June 30, 2026, the Company was in compliance with all of its financial covenants.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;5. Transactions with Affiliated Companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Cash Management Program&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company and its subsidiaries participate in TC Energy&#8217;s cash management program, through TC Energy's subsidiary TCPL USA, which matches short&#8209;term cash surpluses and needs of participating affiliates, thus minimizing total borrowings from outside sources. Monies advanced under the program are considered loans, accruing interest and repayable on demand. The Company receives interest on monies advanced to TCPL USA at the rate of interest earned by TCPL USA on its short-term cash investments. The Company pays interest on monies advanced from TCPL USA based on TCPL USA's short-term borrowing costs. At June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025, the Company had a demand loan receivable balance from TCPL USA of $222.6 million and $189.4 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:10pt;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;b.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.13pt"&gt;Affiliate Revenues and Expenses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Great Lakes Gas Transmission Limited Partnership (GLGT), a TC Energy subsidiary, provides the Company transportation capacity of which the longest agreement extends through 2047. The Company also has natural gas storage contracts with another TC Energy affiliate, Blue Lake Gas Storage Company, and ANR Storage Company, a TC Energy subsidiary. The Company&#8217;s contracts with Blue Lake Gas Storage Company cover a total capacity of 36 Bcf of natural gas storage through March 2031. The Company&#8217;s contract with ANR Storage Company covers a total capacity of 31 Bcf of natural gas storage through March 2028. Transportation and storage costs are recorded as operating expenses. The Company also may provide other affiliates transportation and storage services under terms that are the same as those provided to nonaffiliated parties. In addition, the Company contracts with ANR Storage Company to provide condensate processing services for condensate recovered from the Company&#8217;s storage operations. Proceeds from ANR Storage Company for the sale of the condensate generated from processing are recorded by the Company as revenues from affiliates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Additionally, the Company entered into a transportation agreement with Northern Border Pipeline Company, a TC Energy affiliate, to provide the Company with 203,600 Dth/day of capacity from November 2027 through October 2047 and 76,035 from November 2025 through October 2035.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company is charged by TC Energy for services such as legal, tax, treasury, human resources, other administrative functions, and for other costs incurred on its behalf. These include, but are not limited to, employee benefit costs and property and liability insurance costs. These costs are based on direct assignment to the extent practicable, or by using allocation methods that are reasonable reflections of the utilization of services provided to or for the benefits received by the Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company provides operational and/or administrative services to TC Energy affiliates ANR Storage Company, GLGT, and other affiliates. Service costs are based on direct assignment to the extent practicable, or by using allocation methods that are reasonable reflections of the utilization of services provided to or for the benefits received by the affiliates. The Company records the amounts received for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;these services as a reimbursement of operating expenses and revenues from affiliates in the case of rent charged for use of office space.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The following table shows revenues and charges from/to the Company&#8217;s affiliates for the three and six months ended June 30:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:85.565%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:40.813%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:12.291%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.191%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:12.291%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.191%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:12.291%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.191%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:12.641%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt