    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL (Park and Loan) is a balancing service.&#160; PAL quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote"/>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents regulatory costs associated with the filing of a general rate case. These costs are associated with an ongoing proceeding and are probable for recovery.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">September 29, 2025 in Docket No. RP25-1164.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">March 25, 2026 in Docket No. RP26-586.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">April 30, 2026 in Docket No. RP26-807.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This balance represents the impact of U.S. Tax Reform as applied to businesses subject to rate-regulated accounting, and is being accounted for in accordance with FERC's Policy Statement issued November 15, 2018 in Docket No. PL19.2 and adjusted August 1, 2022 per a rate case settlement in Docket Nos. RP22-501-000 and RP22-501-001. Per the settlement, the Company is amortizing the regulatory liability over 20.15 years beginning August 1, 2022.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate Schedule PAL (Park and Loan) is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent's contract storage volume at June 30, 2026 was 195,291,843 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent's use of system gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent's use of system gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other receipts include linepack and storage adjustments.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent's replacement of system gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent's replacement of system gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other deliveries include linepack, decreases in customer storage, gas sales, gas used for other operations, and&#160; adjustments.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">For each month, lines 11, 18, and 26 are allocated to each rate type: Discounted Rate, Negotiated Rate, and Recourse Rate, using a pro rata allocation.&#160; The pro rata allocation is determined by dividing the gross Shipper Supplied Gas from each rate type by the total Shipper Supplied Gas and multiplied by the corresponding totals for lines 11, 18, and 26.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">For each month, lines 13 and 20 are allocated to each rate type: Discounted Rate, Negotiated Rate, and Recourse Rate, using a pro rata allocation.&#160; The pro rata allocation is determined by dividing the gross Shipper Supplied Gas from each rate type by the total Shipper Supplied Gas and multiplied by the corresponding totals for lines 13 and 20.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">For each month, lines 18 and 20 include fuel paid to others for Discounted, Negotiated and Recourse Rates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">For valuation, a monthly average rate is calculated using the same spot price indexes as ANR&#8217;s cashout mechanism.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">816, 818, 821, 823, 824, 826</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">816, 818, 821, 823, 826</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">816, 818,&#160; 823, 826</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Rate of Return utilized is an actual three year average rate.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ANR Pipeline Company is the entity used as the source of the capital structure figures.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total Cost of Account 123.1 $100</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote"/>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amounts related to uncertain tax positions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total amount relates to MI and OK uncertain tax positions. Reclass also made between jurisdictions to align with the income tax filings.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote"/>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote"/>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Quantities reported represented allocated and billed Dth and do not represent system throughput.&#160; An individual quantity of gas may be reflected in multiple unbundled services prior to final delivery, for example, transmission, no notice balancing, interruptible park and lend, and interruptible wheeling.&#160; Thus, the same quantity of gas may be reflected multiple times so that the quantity by service class can not be added to determine total throughput.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Where transportation services are bundled with storage service, the volumes are reported with transportation.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule IPLS (Park and Loan) is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Discounted and Negotiated Rate Services include all revenues associated with 1) firm contract services with primary route dicounts or negotiated rates and any revenues from capacity releases and 2) discounted routes on interruptible contract services.&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Quantities reported represented allocated and billed Dth and do not represent system throughput.&#160; An individual quantity of gas may be reflected in multiple unbundled services prior to final delivery, for example, transmission, no notice balancing, interruptible wheeling.&#160; Thus, the same quantity of gas may be reflected multiple times so that the quantities by service class cannot be used to determine total throughput.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Imbalance data is reported by service class or rate schedule shown.&#160; For details regarding schedules and zones, see pages 302 through 307.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Receipt&#160; Points: Farwell, South Chester, Deward, Muttonville, MIDelivery Points: Farwell, Fortune Lake, South Chester, Deward, Muttonville, St. Clair, MI</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Receipt Points: Emerson, MIDelivery Points: Fortune Lake, MI</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-40" id="fn-40" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">For comparative purposes to prior filings, the amount Assessed by Regulatory Commision for 2024 including the true-up assesed in 2025 for the prior year was $3,527,638.&#160; The new validation requires the value in this field to equal the Total Expense for Current Year in column (d).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">For comparative purposes to prior filings, the amount Assessed Regulatory Commission for 2025 was $3,493,625.&#160; The new validation requires the value in this field to equal the Total Expense for Current Year in column (d).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-42" id="fn-42" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Total Expense for the Current Year column was repurposed from the total Expenses to Date.&#160; For comparative purposes to prior filings, the $3,527,638 for 2024 has been expensed to date, with $2,645,163 of the amount expensed in 2025.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-43" id="fn-43" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">See Notes to Financial Statements - Transactions with Affiliated Companies for the basis of allocated expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-44" id="fn-44" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">See Notes to Financial Statements - Transactions with Affiliated Companies for the basis of allocated expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-45" id="fn-45" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The conversion factor for Certificated Storage Capacity is 1.020 BTU.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-46" id="fn-46" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The conversion factor for Cushion Gas is 1.020 BTU.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-47" id="fn-47" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Lines 7 and 26 represent total measured transmission system deliveries.&#160; These measured deliveries are pro-rated to No-Notice, Other Firm and Interruptible Transportation based on each categories share of the daily allocated volumes.</link:footnote>
